  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only task-level object and zone search/approach actions, pickup/drop actions, color observations, and the existing claim, release, publish, and received coordination events. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because collision_avoidance already governs them and the objective does not request direct low-level motion control.",
    "transition_design": "States encode remaining boxes and current payload: red is delivered in three one-box batches, green in a two-box batch followed by one box, and blue in one three-box batch. Each branch requires visibility before its initial claim, handles competing claims through wait states, repeats search_object and approach_object during collection, recovers on not-visible and failure observations, and permits reached observations from search or approach states. Matching zone search and approach occur only after the required payload is collected; one drop_object unloads each batch. Intermediate red and green batches use release_red or release_green, while the final color batch publishes its matching delivered event. received_delivered_red, received_delivered_green, and received_delivered_blue advance past work reported complete by the team. Only all_done is marked, so completion requires all three color totals to be accounted for. No low-level collision behavior is added or altered.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
}
